          "text": "The dominant phase indexes on a primitive trigonal cell with \\(a \\approx 9.123\\) \u00c5 and \\(c \\approx 8.534\\) \u00c5. The systematic intensity distribution and composition support the hP20 Sc\\(_7\\)Cl\\(_{12}\\)C-type structure in \\(P\\bar{3}m1\\), with Mn centered in a Tb\\(_6\\) octahedron and one additional axial Tb site. Representative indexed peaks are 001 at 10.36\u00b0, 100 at 11.19\u00b0, 101 at 15.27\u00b0, 002 at 20.81\u00b0, 200 at 22.49\u00b0, 201 at 24.82\u00b0, 112 at 28.62\u00b0, 003 at 31.42\u00b0, 103 at 33.46\u00b0, and 310 at 41.15\u00b0.\n\nThe lattice and structure type are robust; the positional parameters below are a chemically restrained powder model rather than single-crystal-precision coordinates.\n\n```cif\ndata_Tb7MnI12\n_audit_creation_method\n;Powder indexing and constrained direct-space model.\nCu Kalpha1 wavelength = 1.5406 Angstrom.\n;\n_chemical_name_common                 'terbium manganese iodide'\n_chemical_formula_sum                 'Tb7 Mn I12'\n_chemical_formula_structural          'Tb7MnI12'\n_cell_formula_units_Z                  1\n\n_cell_length_a                         9.1232\n_cell_length_b                         9.1232\n_cell_length_c                         8.5335\n_cell_angle_alpha                      90\n_cell_angle_beta                       90\n_cell_angle_gamma                      120\n_cell_volume                           615.1\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt              'P -3 m 1'\n_space_group_IT_number                 164\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type                 'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength           1.5406\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn          7.26\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nTb  0\nMn  0\nI   0\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nMn1  Mn  1  a  0.0000  0.0000  0.0000  1.0  0.8\nTb1  Tb  1  b  0.0000  0.0000  0.5000  1.0  0.8\nTb2  Tb  6  i  0.1375  0.8625  0.1785  1.0  0.8\nI1   I   6  i  0.8200  0.1800  0.3500  1.0  1.0\nI2   I   6  i  0.4600  0.5400  0.0550  1.0  1.0\n```\n\nA closely related surviving symmetry alternative is \\(P\\bar{3}\\) (No. 147), obtained by releasing the mirror restraints \\(y=-x\\) on the three sixfold sites. The powder pattern does not independently justify those additional coordinates, so the higher-symmetry \\(P\\bar{3}m1\\) model is preferred. Several weaker features\u2014notably near 18.98\u00b0, 24.45\u00b0, 26.96\u00b0, 29.59\u00b0, 32.89\u00b0, and 38.49\u00b0\u2014are not accounted for by the principal trigonal lattice and may indicate a minor secondary phase or weak symmetry-lowering/superstructure scattering.",
